  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INTEGRATING SEA TURTLE CONSERVATION AND COMMUNITY WELLBEING AT INDEX SITES IN INDIA TOWARDS THE LONG-TERM SUSTAINABILITY OF COASTAL AND MARINE ECOSYSTEMS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO IMPLEMENT A CONSERVATION PROGRAM FOR SEA TURTLES IN INDIA. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE (1) CONDUCTING AN ANNUAL CENSUS OF THE LARGE OLIVE RIDLEY MASS NESTING POPULATION AT RUSHIKULYA WITH PARTNERS (2) STRENGTHENING A PROGRAM TO MONITOR AND PROTECT THE LEATHERBACK NESTING COLONY IN THE ANDAMAN AND NICOBAR ISLANDS (3) CONDUCTING TRAINING PROGRAMS FOR CAPACITY BUILDING OF A NETWORK OF ORGANIZATIONS CALLED THE TURTLE ACTION GROUP (TAG) TO IMPROVE ORGANIZATIONAL STRENGTHS AND CONSERVATION IMPACTS AND (4) DESIGNING AND DEVELOPING EDUCATIONAL MATERIALS AND DISPLAYS IN COLLABORATION WITH THE FOREST DEPARTMENT.</narrative>
  </description>
